                <pb facs="1144" n="1064" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg1064"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. May to Mr. Bowen.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic">May 1,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay directs Mr. Bowen to say to the Venezuelan Government, without waiving
                    rights already claimed, that upon representations made to the Department of
                    State that the men of the New York and Bermudez Company are without food and are
                    dependent upon provisions on board the <hi rendition="#italic">Viking</hi>, it
                    is urged that, after search for arms and ammunition, the vessel be cleared with
                    an innocent cargo for Caño Colorado, either by the Venezuelan or the United
                    States consul; that an answer is urgently desired.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
